<div class="container mt-4">
    <div class="card shadow p-4">
        <h3 class="text-center">About HeuroLogicV3</h3>
        <p class="text-muted text-center">A Master's Thesis Project</p>

        <p>
            <strong>HeuroLogicV3</strong> is a web application designed to support **decision-making** using the
            **Analytic Hierarchy Process (AHP)**. It was created as part of a **Master's Thesis** in Applied Computer Science.
        </p>

        <h5>📌 Project Information</h5>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Project Title:</strong> HeuroLogicV3</li>
            <li><strong>Author:</strong> Dawid Dojczman</li>
            <li><strong>Student ID:</strong> 112766</li>
            <li><strong>Field of Study:</strong> Applied Computer Science (MSc)</li>
            <li><strong>Thesis Supervisor:</strong> A web-based decision support application based on heuristic methods</li>
            <li><strong>University:</strong> Politechnika Bydgoska im. Jana i Jędrzeja Śniadeckich w Bydgoszczy</li>
        </ul>

        <h5>💡 What is AHP?</h5>
        <p>
            The **Analytic Hierarchy Process (AHP)** is a structured technique for organizing and analyzing complex decisions.
            It allows users to **compare criteria** and **evaluate alternatives** using weighted scores, providing
            a **rational basis for choosing the best option**.
        </p>

        <h5>🚀 Key Features</h5>
        <ul>
            <li>Structured decision-making based on AHP</li>
            <li>Comparison of multiple criteria and alternatives</li>
            <li>Automatic ranking and recommendation</li>
            <li>Secure user authentication & decision history tracking</li>
        </ul>

        <h5>📘 Learn More</h5>
        <p>
            For a detailed guide on using the application, visit our <a href="/user-guide" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary">User Guide</a>.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>
